WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.805
-I think, for a lot of fans of
this show,

00:00:01.805 --> 00:00:04.403
the most exciting thing was
the very fact that there was

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:08.908
a season 4 and that you were,
in fact, alive.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.611
When were you aware that
your character had survived

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:15.081
season 3?

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.083
-Yeah, I was aware
the whole time.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.519
It was -- It wasn't
a secret to me,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:24.257
but, you know, any time
you have an ending like that,

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.193
then you make people wonder.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.528
I think it's always
a good thing

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.029
because, you know,
people are always --

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.298
I think that's the great thing
about these streaming shows,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:37.970
is that it always leaves you
wanting something, you know,

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.438
and I think it's human nature.

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:42.308
It's like why people like
soap operas.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.943
You know, they want to see
what's going to happen

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.780
to Muffy and Biff, or whatever,
you know.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.248
You know, once they announced
that there'd be a season 4,

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:51.884
obviously, everybody knew
that, you know,

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:53.653
I'm probably going to come back,
somehow.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.856
But the way it's done
is pretty interesting,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.093
and it actually started with
Larry Trilling,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:03.062
who's the, you know,
show-runner,

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:06.465
director of the show,
who's a brilliant guy.

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:09.468
And I said, "Look, I'd love to
shoot in San Francisco

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.604
for the last season, and
I'd love to have some kind of

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:16.041
"Vertigo" vibe,
and that's what we did.

00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:19.511
And there's a lot of sort of
spooky stuff in it

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:22.648
that's not your usual,
you know, linear storytelling.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:27.887
You know, and in this case,
it's about the opioid crisis

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:32.024
in this country -- which we
have, [laughs] you know,

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:35.628
and it's a -- it's
a pretty heavy season,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.830
and I think we ended it
on the right note.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.899
I mean, you know,
sometimes I think series

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.235
go a bridge too far,

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.671
and you kind of want to end
on a high note,

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:48.173
you know,
or with your most powerful one.

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:50.176
And of course, you always want
to say the last season

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:54.547
was the best, but in this case,
I truly believe it is.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:58.217
And I'd only signed up
to do four seasons

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.719
and we all agreed that,
you know what?

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:04.924
This is perfect to end it here
because, you know,

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.926
you don't want to be
struggling for a story

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.295
that beats that one
the next year and everything.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.031
So I think we -- I think
we did okay on it.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.967
-One of the other things you had
to keep topping with this show

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:18.004
is these incredible actors
who would come in

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.673
and play villains
over the course of the season.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.677
You had Bill Hurt, Dennis Quaid,
Amy Brenneman last year,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:28.414
and now J.K. Simming--
J.K. Simmons, excuse me,

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.316
and Bruce Dern.
Were those guys that

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.685
you'd worked with in the past?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:36.556
-Yeah, I had done one scene
with J.K. in a movie

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.224
that I starred in years ago

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.860
called "Astronaut Farmer",
and J.K. was in that,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.862
so I knew him a bit.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:47.833
Bruce and I go way, way back,
and he's one of my mentors

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:51.104
and, you know,
people that I hold dear,

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:55.007
and it was great
to be with him again

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.709
because I've done,
you know, four or five things

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.912
with Bruce in the past.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:02.915
And he's wonderful in it.
Both of them are.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.684
It's -- When you've been
in this business a long time,

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:07.620
you kind of know everybody,
you know?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.722
I mean, you and I met
when you were a fledgling

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.390
on "Saturday Night Live".
-My early days.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.627
-Very early days,
-Early, early days, you know.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.796
Bear Research. Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:21.567
-And [clears throat] --
and so, when you're around

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.003
people like that,
sometimes you go,

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:27.106
"Oh my God, that's Bruce Dern."
You know?

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.376
And I knew
Johnny Cash very well,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:34.847
and I -- it was like being
in the room with like, you know,

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.183
Fred Flintstone or something.
It's like, "Are you kidding me?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.618
I'm actually in the room
with Fred Flintstone?

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.954
-Right?
-You know?

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:46.092
-And yeah, Bruce and I have had
an amazing time over the years.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.361
He's been very, very good
to me and a mentor to me.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.330
-Is this a situation based on
your friendship

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.466
that you call them up
and say, "There's a part for you

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:57.169
in this season of 'Goliath'?"
How does it work?

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.104
-Yeah, it kind of works
that way.

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:03.676
You know, Larry said to me,
"You think Bruce would do this?"

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.411
And I said, "I don't know,
I'll call him."

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.913
And he said,
"Yeah, I'd love to."

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.882
Yeah, it was kind of like --
it was that way with Dennis,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:13.986
also, and Dwight Yoakam
in the first season.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:19.292
There are several people
who we've sort of talked over

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.227
over the years in the series

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.296
and since had
a personal connection with them.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:28.133
Like in season two and three,
we had Paul Williams.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.270
You know,
and he was a buddy of mine,

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.208
and they said, "Who would you
get to play this part?"

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.509
And I said, "Paul Williams."

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.144
They said,
"You mean the songwriter?"

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:41.614
I go, "Yeah, trust me."

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.816
-Well, I guess the first time
I saw Dwight Yoakam act

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.951
was probably "Sling Blade",
right?

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:48.320
I mean, had he done anything
before that?

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.824
-He had. He'd done a couple of,
you know, independent films.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:54.426
And Dwight --
actually, it's funny

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:58.464
because I started out in music
and became an actor,

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:02.134
and Dwight started out in the
theater program at Ohio State

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:03.535
and became a musician.

00:05:03.535 --> 00:05:08.173
You know,
it was really funny, but...

00:05:08.173 --> 00:05:10.943
Dwight was a good actor. I mean,
I'd seen the, you know,

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.579
smaller things he'd done
before we did "Sling Blade",

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:18.384
and I knew he was --
he was a dandy.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.553
-He must -- I'm assuming
he's a far nicer person

00:05:21.553 --> 00:05:22.955
than he came off in
"Sling Blade",

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.824
because I got to be honest,

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:27.426
I was really happy how it ended
for him in that movie.

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.094
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:31.997
Dwight -- Dwight did a great job
as an ass [bleep].

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:33.599
He sure did.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:34.633
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.135
Oh, and I have to say, I mean,

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:41.240
before we get off of this thing,
I kind of like this Zoom idea.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.243
You know, it's not a bad thing.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.812
And the main reason
is because I don't really

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:50.282
like to wear pants.
-Yep.

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:55.354
And, I -- You know, well,
I won't -- I won't say

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.322
the rest of it, but --
-I think we got it.

00:05:57.322 --> 00:05:59.424
I think we can all finish it
from there, yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:05:59.424 --> 00:06:00.759
-Well, I think we can.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.462
You know, you just put
a big flannel jacket on

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:04.997
and enjoy yourself.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:07.566
[ Laughs ] Well, I think we've
all enjoyed ourselves

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:09.335
and it's always great
to see you.

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:10.770
You know what?
And when we're in studio,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.440
we'll figure out a pants-free
existence for you here, too.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.975
-Absolutely. You can just --
You know how you guys, like,

00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:18.644
you know, blank stuff out?

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.046
-Yeah, we'll just blur it.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.781
All right. Thanks, Billy Bob.
Always a pleasure.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.315
The fourth and final season of
"Goliath"

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:25.051
is available now
on Amazon Prime Video.

